  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given binary strings SSS and TTT, each of length NNN, and an integer KKK.\n\nFind whether it is possible to convert string SSS to TTT by making **exactly** KKK operations of the following type:\n\n\nChoose **distinct** indices iii and j&nbsp;(1≤i,j≤N)j \\ (1\\le i, j \\le N)j&nbsp;(1≤i,j≤N);\nSwap SiS_iSi​ with SjS_jSj​.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer T′T'T′, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of the string and the number of operations, respectively.\nThe second line contains the binary string SSS of length NNN.\nThe third line contains the binary string TTT of length NNN.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, `YES`, if it is possible to convert string SSS to TTT by making **exactly** KKK operations. Otherwise, output `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `YES`, `yEs`, `yes`, and `yeS` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T′≤12001 \\leq T' \\leq 12001≤T′≤1200",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N",
      "Si,Ti∈{0,1}S_i, T_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​,Ti​∈{0,1}",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2 2\n01\n10\n2 2\n00\n01\n3 1\n001\n010\n4 2\n1101\n0111",
        "output": "NO\nNO\nYES\nYES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only operation we can perform on SSS is swapping S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​. Thus, performing 222 operations would convert SSS as 01→10→0101 \\rightarrow 10 \\rightarrow 0101→10→01, which is not equal to TTT.\nTest case 222: It is not possible to convert SSS to TTT using any number of operations.\nTest case 333: We can convert string S=001S = 001S=001 to T=010T = 010T=010 using K=1K = 1K=1 operation:\n\nSelect indices i=2i = 2i=2 and j=3j = 3j=3 and swap S2S_2S2​ and S3S_3S3​.\n\nTest case 444: We can convert string S=1101S = 1101S=1101 to T=0111T = 0111T=0111 using K=2K = 2K=2 operations:\n\nSelect indices i=3i = 3i=3 and j=4j = 4j=4 and swap S3S_3S3​ and S4S_4S4​ to obtain 111011101110.\nSelect indices i=1i = 1i=1 and j=4j = 4j=4 and swap S1S_1S1​ and S4S_4S4​ to obtain 011101110111, which is same as TTT."
      }
    ]
  },
